        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF155 adds support for a <code class=\"notranslate\">WebTransport</code> client to specify a list of preferred application-specific protocols in the constructor, and for the server to return its preferred option in <code class=\"notranslate\">WebTransport.protocol</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the release note.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5234310944\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45302\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45302/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45302\">#45302</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45366",
            "title": "FF155 Relnote: WebTransport application-specific protocols",
            "date_modified": "2026-08-28T06:36:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-08-28T06:32:06.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF155 adds support for a <code class=\"notranslate\">WebTransport</code> app to specify a list of preferred application-specific protocols in the constructor, and for the server to return its preferred option in <code class=\"notranslate\">WebTransport.protocol</code>. This documents both parts of that story and adds a section in the guide.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note, what this does not do is explain the underlying browser and server mechanisms for sharing the data. That's not needed in the Web API docs, but would be useful for a server developer. However we don't have any of that context for WebTransport and I don't think is in scope for this task.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"5234310944\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45302\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/45302/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45302\">#45302</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45365",
